A||N||6||polomeno||Draw on battery caused by trunk. light... how to disconnect?||||1||
Z||000000||polomeno||11-21-2000||08:48 PM||||Hey guys.. i have a draw on my battery that i *think* is being casued by my trunk light.. when i pull the fuse that runs the interior lights, lighter and trunk the draw is gone. My trunk light is not connected at all.. there are 2 wires going to the trunk switch ( orange & green ) they are both cut and not connected .. not sure where the short might be but is it ok to just cut them off at the source and tape them up?  any one else had this kinda of problem?<P>thanks<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||11-21-2000||11:42 PM||||what book are you looking at? the lighter and trunk light aren't on the same fuse.<P>lighter is on the 25A bat fuse. the trunk light is on the 20A ctsy/lid fuse.<P>If the switch isn't connected and the light isn't on........ look else where. that trunk light would have to be on on for quite some time to kill the battery.<P>like the lighter. They commonly go bad. take out the black trim over it then take out the socket and uplug it.<P>The BAT fuse will always show some a load on it. the radio is on it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||polomeno||11-22-2000||01:00 AM||||it's not at all connected to the back socket of the trunk lighter.. that's why i watned to know if i could just cut the wires and tape them ????||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||11-22-2000||12:45 PM||||Check the decklid ajar switch, I think it turns on/off the trunk light.  It's near the drivers side rear shock tower.  Press it down, I believe the trunk light should go out if that switch is ok.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-22-2000||01:32 PM||||it would be better to put them back on the switch. Otherwise cap/tape the ends, roll them up and tape them to the harness don't cut them off.||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||11-23-2000||10:07 PM||||i wish my trunk light would work.  the bulb is good, fuse is good, and i couldn't find any wires that might be cut.  any thoughts?<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||11-24-2000||02:36 PM||||S, the switch is shot. it's either on the left side of the trunk wall or on the latch depending what year you have. If it's the one on the latch there's also a connector near the right hinge with 3 or 4 wires.||||reg||1
